        a(f"Capacity = G (T_limit - T_sink) - P0, full fan, pump at the floor, T_sink the air temperature at the radiators (not measured; the fitted Ta {x['Ta']:.0f} C is the effective sink and only the intercept Ta + P0/G is identified). The earlier 518 W at 46 C used the model G at the pump floor ({base['G']['full_pump_floor']:.1f} W/K) built on the pump coefficient gamma = {x['gamma']:.2f}, which is not interpretable (4.1); G 23.8 W/K (pump 100 %) gives {23.8 * 21:.0f} W and the low end of the interval, 22.3 W/K, gives {22.3 * 21:.0f} W at sink 25 C.\n")
        a(tab(["G used", "sink C", "capacity at 46 C W", "capacity at 48 C W", "capacity at 50 C W", "steady Tw at 500 W C", f"steady Tw at peak load {E['peaks']['cpu_max_w'] + self.cfg['ext']['sinks']['peak_gpu_rated_w']:.0f} W C"], [[r["g_label"], f"{r['sink_c']:.0f}", f"{r['cap_46_w']:.0f}", f"{r['cap_48_w']:.0f}", f"{r['cap_50_w']:.0f}", f"{r['steady_500_c']:.1f}", f"{r['steady_peak_c']:.1f}"] for r in rows]))
        r25 = next(r for r in rows if r["g_label"].startswith("G 23.8") and r["sink_c"] == 25.0)
        a(f"\nPeak load context: the highest CPU package power seen is {E['peaks']['cpu_max_w']:.0f} W and the GPU board is rated {self.cfg['ext']['sinks']['peak_gpu_rated_w']:.0f} W (seen {E['peaks']['gpu_max_w']:.0f} W), together about {E['peaks']['cpu_max_w'] + self.cfg['ext']['sinks']['peak_gpu_rated_w']:.0f} W, which steadies at {r25['steady_peak_c']:.1f} C even at a 25 C sink. The highest total heat observed is {E['peaks']['q_max_w']:.0f} W (99.9th percentile {E['peaks']['q_p999_w']:.0f} W). The data hold no summer sink; the table above is a model extrapolation in the sink, with each K of warmer sink costing about 24 W of capacity.\n")
        a("**Plainly: at full fan nothing defends 50 C.** Once the heat exceeds the capacity at 50 C the fan is already at its limit, the 48 C firmware takeover adds nothing, `water_top_limit` is an alarm only, and the manual's coolant limit is 50 C (`snapshot/d5-control.md`). Under a warm summer sink or a combined CPU and GPU peak the only remaining defence is lowering the load, which nothing in the current design does. This is a capacity limit of the radiators, not a setting.\n")

